division:
    an inverse operation of multiplication 

    division breaks a larger number into a group of smaller numbers of identical size(quotient)

it gives us a quotient 

let say we want 15 apples and there are baskets each contains 5 apples,
    how many basket should we take?
    we simply:
        15 / 5 = 3
            15 -> dividend {the total}
            5 -> divisor {thde known int/number}
            3 -> quotient {the unknown number}

represented by:
    a division sign(dot above a line and a dot below the line)
    a slash / angled line 
    a horizontal line 


    15/5 = 3
        the 1st number should be divided by the 2nd (15 divided by 5)
        numerater = divident 
        denomenator = divisor 


